      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Understood, let's enhance the recipe's thoroughness without compromising readability:\n\n---\n\n**Enhanced and Thorough Bread Recipe**\n\n**Ingredients:**\n- All-purpose flour (2 cups)\n- Water (1 1/2 cups)\n- Fine salt (1 1/2 teaspoons)\n- Unsalted butter (1 tablespoon, melted)\n- [Optional] Extra salt for sprinkling (1/4 teaspoon)\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. In a medium-sized bowl, blend 2 cups of all-purpose flour and 1 1/2 teaspoons of fine salt, ensuring a consistent mix.\n2. Slowly introduce 1 1/2 cups of water to the dry ingredients. Stir until you have a smooth, lumpy batter.\n3. Melt 1 tablespoon of unsalted butter carefully. This addition helps to keep the bread moist. Introducing melted butter towards the end prevents greasiness.\n4. Preheat a large non-stick pan over medium heat. If your pan has a lid, now is an ideal time to use it as you'll need it shortly.\n5. Grease the pan lightly with a thin layer of oil. Swirl the butter in the melted butter you've prepared, taking care to distribute it evenly.\n6. Carefully pour the batter",
